@TA_LS_SCARLET_ABANDONED_MANSION_DIARY_PAGE_1
SETCOLOR LSScarletLaylaColor
PRINTFORML %BREAKENG(@"Lunasa did something bad today and Father was quite stern. Usually, it is something that Merlin or Lyrica have done, and I think he is used to punishing them by now, but he was temperate with Lunasa. He didn't lay a hand on her or raise his voice, but I think she took it badly anyway because she has shut herself in her chamber all afternoon and will not answer when I call her.")%
PRINTL
PRINTFORM Poor Lunasa! Since Father went out again, Merlin has been 
CALL COLORMESSAGE("sitting outside of her chamber and blowing a trumpet",LSScarletColor)
PRINTFORML  to cheer her up.
PRINTFORML The noise is completely terrible, of course, because she does not know how to play. Even Lyrica has left her alone by now.
PRINTL
PRINTFORML %BREAKENG(@"I think it is awful what happened because Lunasa did not mean anything wrong. She only wanted to show me one of the items that Father has brought back. He says they are magic and from distant lands, and even from other worlds. There are some even from a place that is at the very most eastern part of the world, where they create such beautiful art, but Father said Lunasa should not have touched it without permission. He said that it is very dangerous, and then he locked it all away in a safe.")%
PRINTL
PRINTFORM Well! I think that will not stop curious Lyrica and Merlin. I expect 
CALL COLORMESSAGE("one of them will find out the code",LSScarletColor)
PRINTFORML , and it will be Lyrica's idea in any case.
PRINTL
PRINTFORML Speaking of Lyrica, I think I will see where she has got to now.
PRINTFORM She hates it very much when we are sad or separated, so I am sure I will find her sulking and 
CALL COLORMESSAGE("petting her puppy in the garden",LSScarletColor)
PRINTFORML .
RESETCOLOR
RETURN

@TA_LS_SCARLET_ABANDONED_MANSION_DIARY_PAGE_2
SETCOLOR LSScarletLaylaColor
PRINTFORML %BREAKENG(@"Lunasa is in better spirits now and I think it is because of Merlin. As I thought, Father has allowed us to look at his collection under supervision. There so many things, I do not know what to write about. I think they are all magic. When I hold each one, I feel as if I can hear the voices of people from far away, speaking in languages I have never heard.")%
PRINTL
PRINTFORML %BREAKENG(@"Lyrica said the items are haunted. Father said the people from the eastern country believe in spirits that live inside of everything, even cups and blades of grass. Merlin pretended she could hear them, too, but Lunasa and Lyrica and Father couldn't hear anything, and besides, I do not think they are spirits talking, anyway.")%
PRINTL
PRINTFORML %BREAKENG(@"It is very hard to explain. The voices I am hearing are not really voices, not that I can hear with my ears anyway, but I am sure they come from real people. With my own soul, I am perceiving their most important sounds: The words of loved ones, or the familiar noises of their favorite places.")%
PRINTFORM When I listen to their happy memories, 
CALL COLORMESSAGE("I become happy myself",LSScarletColor)
PRINTFORM . When I listen to the sad ones, 
CALL COLORMESSAGE("I become sad",LSScarletColor)
PRINTFORML .
PRINTFORM These items are very old, so they must be of people who are already long since dead; 
CALL COLORMESSAGE("illusionary sounds",LSScarletColor)
PRINTFORML  forgotten by everyone alive.
PRINTL
PRINTFORML %BREAKENG(@"Why can only I hear them? Lunasa thinks I am being silly and making it up, but Father was excited. He says that sometimes, magical abilities can awaken in people who come into contact with magic. Maybe I have a gift.")%
PRINTL
PRINTFORML %BREAKENG(@"I rather like the things from that country now, and I have asked Father if I can look at them every day. After seeing that I have an ability, he could not refuse, but sadly for him, he had to give the same permission to my sisters, as well.")%
PRINTFORML %BREAKENG(@"Of course, he will not let Merlin touch anything without him watching, but he trusts Lunasa completely.")%
PRINTL
PRINTFORML %BREAKENG(@"Lyrica wanted to read the books, but Father wouldn't allow it from any of us. He said that one of of them was brought here from the depths of a wicked world of devils. He said that even reading it might curse us and ensnare our souls. Of course, that will never be the end of it because Lyrica has no restraint.")%
PRINTFORM Oh, Father, 
CALL COLORMESSAGE("you will be quite furious again",LSScarletColor)
PRINTFORML  soon!
RESETCOLOR
RETURN

@TA_LS_SCARLET_ABANDONED_MANSION_DIARY_PAGE_3
SETCOLOR LSScarletLaylaColor
PRINTFORML %BREAKENG(@"I have not written for a long time because Father is gone. I will not write what happened because I do not want to remember it.")%
PRINTL
PRINTFORML %BREAKENG(@"In the days that followed, Lyrica spent most of her time in the garden near his grave. Merlin went out all day and did not come back until after dark. Lunasa tried to take care of us, but she hardly spoke a word.")%
PRINTL
PRINTFORML %BREAKENG(@"Everyone has long since gone away. I asked them all to stay and rebuild the house, but no one could bear it. They have forgotten about the good times we have shared and only think about the end.")%
PRINTL
PRINTFORML %BREAKENG(@"Lunasa does not remember the first chocolate cake we made together for Merlin's birthday. Merlin does not remember pulling down the panties of an older girl who was teasing Lyrica for being short. Lyrica does not remember giving Lunasa her shoulder when her heart was in pain.")%
PRINTL
PRINTFORML %BREAKENG(@"None of them remember playing together during music lessons, creating an awful racket and doing everything but learn the instruments. No one but me. I often wonder if there are precious moments that even I have forgotten.")%
PRINTL
PRINTFORML %BREAKENG(@"Days pass meaninglessly. I cannot find the will to rise in the morning. Who will be waiting for me? Whose lively and spirited voices will I hear as anything more than a pale shade of years gone by?")%
PRINTL
PRINTFORML %BREAKENG(@"I do not wish us to end this way. I do not wish to be left without my family, alone until I die. Yet only I can hear my own conjury, and I cannot see nor touch those fleeting phantoms of the past. My strongest power cannot revive those times alone.")%
PRINTL
PRINTFORML %BREAKENG(@"The book that Father had forbidden us to read is written in a magic ink. It is said that words written in that ink can manipulate souls and fate itself. I think I will read my diary again and I will write over my most precious memories in that ink.")%
PRINTL
PRINTFORML %BREAKENG(@"In『reality』, we can never be a family again. If that is the case, let me live inside a fantasy. I have no need for this world anymore.")%
RESETCOLOR
RETURN

@TA_LS_SCARLET_ABANDONED_MANSION_DIARY_PAGE_4
SETCOLOR LSScarletLaylaColor
PRINTFORM Lunasa, 
CALL COLORMESSAGE("you made a beautiful cake today",LSScarletColor)
PRINTFORML , just the way I taught you. Is it not wonderful that your favorite is still chocolate?
PRINTFORML %BREAKENG(@"Compared with the chaos of our sisters, it makes my heart glad to see you never change. Your kindness and thoughtfulness are what support our lives, and I want you to always remember that.")%
PRINTL
PRINTFORM I had not realized, Merlin, that you had returned to gardening, and you had 
CALL COLORMESSAGE("grown your own strawberries",LSScarletColor)
PRINTFORML  to decorate the cake.
PRINTFORML I asked, whatever happened to painting? It was not long ago that you had done nothing but color up everything in the house.
PRINTFORM Such surreal yet wonderfully moving pieces you made, on easels, walls, floors, and even 
CALL COLORMESSAGE("your own naked body",LSScarletColor)
PRINTFORML !
PRINTFORML To that, you said that one cannot eat paint, and so you have had enough of that. I do love your mind, Merlin!
PRINTL
PRINTFORM And Lyrica, oh Lyrica! After cake, 
CALL COLORMESSAGE("we talked in the way that we always used to",LSScarletColor)
PRINTFORML . We played together and spoke of the past.
PRINTFORML %BREAKENG(@"You always understand me, Lyrica. You always heal my heart, even in ways that Merlin cannot. Where would I, or any of us be without you? I want you to always be there for our family, just as you have been until now.")%
PRINTL
PRINTFORML %BREAKENG(@"I know you all have not changed, and neither have I. Soon I will travel very far, and when I come back to you, you will be just the same as you were today. I hope we will have days like this forever.")%
RESETCOLOR
RETURN

