@TA_LS_SCARLET_ABANDONED_MANSION_COUNT_QUESTIONS
PRINTL
{
	CALL ASK_M(
		"What are you?",1,
		"Who created you?",1,
		"Who is Layla?",1,
		"I came to buy some ink",1,
		"That's all",1,
	)
}
PRINTL
SELECTCASE RESULT
	CASE 0
		PRINTFORMW 「A failed poltergeist. A spirit creation of a man who my creators never knew. All that I am is based on memories written in a book.」
		PRINTFORMW 「Yet I cannot imagine my creation was intentional, nor that of the other phantoms around. We are by-products of the meanderings of amateurs.」
		PRINTFORMW 「My Layla's diary is the core of my existence, yet without any『truth』to support that existence, I shall soon fade away.」
		PRINTFORMW 「...That is the nature of the『magic』from whence I and my creators are born.」
	CASE 1
		PRINTFORMW 「My daughters... or so they look. In truth, they are the same as I am, though more complete.」
		PRINTFORMW 「Oh, but I love them... I have no right to call myself their father, yet still!」
		PRINTFORMDW The Count makes a shaking fist, and his voice sounds strained.
		PRINTL
		PRINTFORMW 「The diary that forms my『core』is the source of that love. It is the reason for my very being.」
	CASE 2
		PRINTFORMW 「The only one of my daughters whose voice yet does not grace this home. It is she who created her sisters, the poltergeists. She died long ago.」
		PRINTFORMW 「I believe those three are now trying to imitate the process of their own birth in order to revive her memory. That is how I was born.」
		PRINTL
		PRINTFORMDW The count drifts towards the outside window, and into the scarlet light. He stares up above with no expression, yet a tightness in his posture.
		PRINTFORM 「Yet, that accursed 
		SETCOLOR LSScarletColor
		PRINTFORM scarlet moon
		SETCOLOR LSScarletCountColor
		PRINTFORMW  corrupted our minds as I was taking form.」
		PRINTL
		PRINTFORMDW In other words, they were trying to conjure poltergeists right as you signed the contract?
		PRINTFORMW 「It is surely a devil's foul twisting of our fate, for it has plunged our souls into an unending torment!」
	CASE 3
		PRINTFORMW 「...A devil's magic ink that binds the soul with written words. What better medium for the conjuring of poltergeists?」
		PRINTFORMW 「By writing out one's memories of someone who once lived, one might create a facsimile. I believe my daughters did something to that effect.」
		PRINTFORMW 「But only by my Layla's power could one truly...」
		PRINTL
		PRINTFORMW 「...Listen to me. The three poltergeist sisters are trapped inside of madness. They have failed to conjure their sister, my Layla.」
		PRINTFORMW 「Because of the moon, their loving memories have been twisted into something base. Vile temptation invades their thoughts and leads them astray.」
		PRINTFORMW 「Their true memories; memories written by Layla of their original selves; and new, false memories created by the moon...」
		PRINTFORMW 「All vie together, and the moon prevails.」
		PRINTFORMW 「I am but a powerless failed poltergeist. There is naught I can do, and I do not know if I can face them, or I may go mad again, myself.」
		PRINTFORMW 「You must go in my place. Force them to reckon with their true memories, or else they shall be cursed forever!」
		PRINTL
		PRINTFORMW 「I know I am not their father. I know they are not the daughters of this house. I know that the Prismriver family is gone.」
		PRINTFORMW 「Still, I must not leave this world before I see this done. No matter if these feelings and connections are false, they are mine!」
		PRINTFORMW 「Do this and you shall have your inkpot. I swear to it!」
		IF !GETBIT(QUEST_FLAG(LSScarletAlias,QLSScarletAM),QBitLSScarletAMPhotoOfLayla)
			PRINTL
			PRINTFORMDW The Count drifts towards the desk, produces a key from his pocket, and unlocks a drawer from which he pulls a small photo frame.
			PRINTFORMDW He then floats over and hands it to you. In it, you can see a young girl in a frilled dress, in black and white.
			PRINTL
			PRINTFORMW 「This is my Layla's true face. If the sisters see this, they might realize, as I have, that you are not her.」
			PRINTFORMW 「...Though, if even I did not realize, it may not be so. If their grasp on reality is truly so dire, beware.」
			PRINTL
			PRINTFORMDW Received the photo of Layla Prismriver.
			CALL SET_QUEST_FLAG(LSScarletAlias,QLSScarletAM,QBitLSScarletAMPhotoOfLayla,1)
		ENDIF
	CASE 4
		RETURN
ENDSELECT
RESTART

@TA_LS_SCARLET_ABANDONED_MANSION_COUNTS_ROOM_COMMAND_USE(CommandTarget,FullCommand)
#DIMS DYNAMIC CommandTarget
#DIMS DYNAMIC FullCommand
SELECTCASE CommandTarget
	CASE "book"
		SIF !GETBIT(QUEST_FLAG(LSScarletAlias,QLSScarletAM),QBitLSScarletAMDevilBook)
			GOTO FAIL
		IF GETBIT(QUEST_FLAG(LSScarletAlias,QLSScarletAM),QBitLSScarletAMPhotoOfLayla)
			PRINTFORMDW You've already shown him the devil's book.
			GOTO SUCCEED
		ENDIF
		SETCOLOR LSScarletCountColor
		PRINTFORMW 「What is that?! Is that not a treasure of mine? That was in my safe! You dare to disobey your father?!」
		PRINTFORMW 「I expressly forbade you to take the book, but you did it anyway! You know very well what could happen! You saw it happen to me!」
		PRINTFORMW 「It happened! It already happened! But this has never happened, or has it...?」
		PRINTFORMDW The shadow grips the sides of his head as he stares at the book in your hands, trying desperately to form a coherent thought.
		PRINTL
		PRINTFORMW 「Aaaaargh! Begone, devil! Begone, devil! Begone, devil! Begone, devil! Begone, devil! Begone, devil! Begone, devil!」
		PRINTL
		{
			CALL ASK_M(
				"I'm not who you think I am",1,
				"You aren't possessed, you're confused",1,
				"This book isn't real, and neither are you",1,
			)
		}
		PRINTL
		SELECTCASE RESULT
			CASE 0
				PRINTFORMW 「I know... I know, because I know her face, even though I do not remember...」
			CASE 1
				PRINTFORMW 「Not possessed...? Blast it, this red light... Indeed, it must be the cause. It was never so sickening...」
